{"ticker":"KIM","name":"Kimco Realty Corporation","sector":"Real Estate","industry":"REIT - Retail","country":"United States","price":{"last":23.4,"market_cap":15696471040,"pe_ratio":27.529411,"high_52w":26.65,"low_52w":19.76,"shares_outstanding":670789373,"beta":0.965,"as_of":"2026-10-28"},"stats":{"forward_pe":26.072424,"ps_ratio":7.1767306,"pb_ratio":1.527814,"enterprise_value":24010377216,"ev_ebitda":18.024,"peg":null,"roe":0.05806,"roa":0.023740001,"gross_margin":0.68933,"eps":0.85,"forward_eps":0.8975,"avg_50":23.066,"avg_200":23.4779,"target_mean":25.82143,"analyst_count":21,"rating":"buy","target_low":23.0,"target_high":30.0,"prev_close":23.7,"day_low":23.345,"day_high":23.695,"volume":7494899},"profile":{"description":"Kimco Realty is a real estate investment trust (REIT) and leading owner and operator of high-quality, open-air, grocery-anchored shopping centers and mixed-use properties in the United States. The company's portfolio is strategically concentrated in the first-ring suburbs of the top major metropolitan markets, including high-barrier-to-entry coastal markets and Sun Belt cities. Its tenant mix is focused on essential, necessity-based goods and services that drive multiple shopping trips per week. Publicly traded on the NYSE since 1991 and included in the S&P 500 Index, the company has specialized in shopping center ownership, management, acquisitions, and value-enhancing redevelopment activities for more than 65 years. With a proven commitment to corporate responsibility, Kimco Realty is a recognized industry leader in this area. As of June 30, 2026, the company owned interests in 564 U.S. shopping centers and mixed-use assets comprising 100 million square feet of gross leasable space. Kimco Realty Corporation was incorporated in 1958 in Maryland and is based in Jericho, New York.","employees":710,"website":"https://www.kimcorealty.com"},"financials":{"revenue":{"2022":1727684000.0,"2023":1783400000.0,"2024":2037014000.0,"2025":2140116000.0},"